      "tag": "nit",
      "description": "The `review-accepted` waiver applies to the newest summary review, not to the head commit that review saw. Non-owner PRs get no push marker and no review on a push. So if the PR's author pushes after the operator adds the label, the label still holds and the PR reads `ready` on unreviewed code, where it used to stay `review-open`. Gating on the head having a `claude-review` status (`accepted = review !== undefined && acceptedSince(...)`) would close this.",
